thread:
sam: Drafting a small docs change to demonstrate compact envelopes + union-array items for tool-calling. want to show canonical + compact examples and a tiny JS parsing hint. opening PR in a bit.

hana: can you paste the exact schema you plan to use? i'll make sure the snippet matches the parser tests.

sam: yep — minimal schema: an object with `ops` array where each item can be a string or an object with `action`+`args`. idea is to show both:

```
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "ops": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "oneOf": [
          { "type": "string" },
          {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "action": { "type": "string" },
              "args": { "type": "object" }
            },
            "required": ["action"]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["ops"]
}
```

sam: canonical example output:
```
{ "ops": ["noop", {"action":"email","args":{"to":"x@example.com"}} ] }
```

sam: compact envelope example (single-line, minimal whitespace) that we want to mention for low-latency callers:
```
{"o":["noop",{"a":"email","arg":{"t":"x@example.com"}}]}
```

leo: fyi parser tests fail if outer text isn't stripped, so include a note: call `stripOuterText: true` in the SDK helper or use our `parseWithFallback` helper.

hana: small UX note: suggest we avoid spaces in keys (e.g., `Action Name`) — that broke some regex routes in production. add a one-liner about tokenization-friendly keys.

docs-bot: PR queued by sam: <https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1290|#1290> — reviewers: @hana, @leo.

rachel: i'll take the link fixes sweep. there's an old anchor on the function-calling page that points to `#call-flow` instead of `#toolflow` — will patch in the PR. also adding a migration note for Dedicated customers who pinned models with different strictness.

sam: thanks everyone. aim to convert to ready-for-review after comments. quick checklist in PR description: 1) add canonical + compact examples, 2) SDK snippet w/ `parseWithFallback` + options, 3) migration note for pinned models, 4) anchor/link fixes.

leo: LGTM overall, will leave a couple tiny wording nits. :+1:

hana: will run parser harness once the PR is up.

sam: filing now, pinging reviewers. cheers! :rocket:
